LSTC is a compiled language with the goal of making programming (system or software) easier
(primarily because of some poorly implemented libraries, strange API, too many external dependencies
or complex memory management) The name comes from one of my (currently private) projects called L$script,
its a bytecode-based language (similar to java), yet, I thought "why not make it compiled?",
and focused on this project, LSTC - L$Script type compiled (or "lets skip the C" on a good day, on an
even better day "LSTC surpasses the C")
